**One thing to know:** what you can read depends heavily on the platform. iOS exposes far less than Android (no IMEI, serial, MAC, installed app list, or detailed per-app stats), and newer Android versions restrict IMEI, serial, MAC, installed apps, and background location behind special permissions or system-app status. Web apps are limited to what browser APIs expose. Because device identifiers are sensitive, request permissions only when a specific tool needs them, mask IDs by default when sharing, and avoid sending any of it off-device without clear consent (Play Store policy and GDPR both care about this).

